SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Do not attempt to feed the infant any standard formula or breast milk under any circumstances. They will require a highly specialized, synthetic medical diet for life.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The baby's body is completely missing the enzymes needed to break down certain proteins in his milk. Because he cannot break them down, they are building up to massive, toxic levels, causing his brain to swell, dropping his blood sugar, and creating that sweet smell. The glucose gel stops his body from breaking down its own muscle, but he needs emergency hospital treatment to wash the toxins out of his blood.
Actionable Steps: Stop all normal feeding immediately. Pack a hospital bag. Follow all instructions from the emergency medical team implicitly.

